From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the generated colorimetry data when cross compiling

data/cmf and data/illuminant convert their CSV sources by running the
cd-it8 that was just built - and that binary is for the target, so meson
stops at configure time:

    ERROR: An exe_wrapper is needed for .../client/cd-it8 but was not
    found. Please define one in cross file and check the command and/or
    add it to PATH.

A host cd-it8 is not a practical way out: colord asks for gusb, gudev
and libudev unconditionally at the top of meson.build, so building the
library it links against for the build machine would mean host variants
of all three, and libgudev wants udev itself.

Dropping the files costs nothing here. They are reference spectra and
colour matching functions for calibrating a display against a measuring
instrument; nothing in colord reads them from where they install - only
the test suite loads them, and out of the build directory - and this
build already has argyllcms_sensor disabled, so there is no instrument
to calibrate against in the first place.

--- a/data/cmf/meson.build
+++ b/data/cmf/meson.build
@@ -1,9 +1,22 @@
-foreach arg: [ 'CIE1964-10deg-XYZ', 'CIE1931-2deg-XYZ' ]
-  custom_target(arg,
-    input: arg + '.csv',
-    output: arg + '.cmf',
-    command: [ cd_idt8, 'create-cmf', '@OUTPUT@', '@INPUT@', '1.0' ],
-    install: true,
-    install_dir: join_paths(datadir, 'colord', 'cmf')
-  )
-endforeach
+# cd-it8 is built for the target, so a cross build cannot run it to convert
+# these CSVs:
+#
+#   ERROR: An exe_wrapper is needed for .../client/cd-it8 but was not
+#   found. Please define one in cross file and check the command and/or
+#   add it to PATH.
+#
+# The outputs are reference data for calibrating against a measuring
+# instrument. Nothing in colord loads them from their installed location -
+# only the test suite reads them, out of the build directory - and a build
+# with argyllcms_sensor disabled has no sensor to calibrate with.
+if not meson.is_cross_build()
+  foreach arg: [ 'CIE1964-10deg-XYZ', 'CIE1931-2deg-XYZ' ]
+    custom_target(arg,
+      input: arg + '.csv',
+      output: arg + '.cmf',
+      command: [ cd_idt8, 'create-cmf', '@OUTPUT@', '@INPUT@', '1.0' ],
+      install: true,
+      install_dir: join_paths(datadir, 'colord', 'cmf')
+    )
+  endforeach
+endif
--- a/data/illuminant/meson.build
+++ b/data/illuminant/meson.build
@@ -1,31 +1,44 @@
-generated_spectra = [
-  'CIE-A',
-  'CIE-B',
-  'CIE-C',
-  'CIE-D50',
-  'CIE-D55',
-  'CIE-D65',
-  'CIE-D93',
-  'CIE-E',
-  'CIE-F10',
-  'CIE-F11',
-  'CIE-F12',
-  'CIE-F1',
-  'CIE-F2',
-  'CIE-F3',
-  'CIE-F4',
-  'CIE-F5',
-  'CIE-F6',
-  'CIE-F7',
-  'CIE-F8',
-  'CIE-F9',
-]
-foreach arg: generated_spectra
-  custom_target(arg,
-    input: arg + '.csv',
-    output: arg + '.sp',
-    command: [ cd_idt8, 'create-sp', '@OUTPUT@', '@INPUT@', '100.0' ],
-    install: true,
-    install_dir: join_paths(datadir, 'colord', 'illuminant')
-  )
-endforeach
+# cd-it8 is built for the target, so a cross build cannot run it to convert
+# these CSVs:
+#
+#   ERROR: An exe_wrapper is needed for .../client/cd-it8 but was not
+#   found. Please define one in cross file and check the command and/or
+#   add it to PATH.
+#
+# The outputs are reference data for calibrating against a measuring
+# instrument. Nothing in colord loads them from their installed location -
+# only the test suite reads them, out of the build directory - and a build
+# with argyllcms_sensor disabled has no sensor to calibrate with.
+if not meson.is_cross_build()
+  generated_spectra = [
+    'CIE-A',
+    'CIE-B',
+    'CIE-C',
+    'CIE-D50',
+    'CIE-D55',
+    'CIE-D65',
+    'CIE-D93',
+    'CIE-E',
+    'CIE-F10',
+    'CIE-F11',
+    'CIE-F12',
+    'CIE-F1',
+    'CIE-F2',
+    'CIE-F3',
+    'CIE-F4',
+    'CIE-F5',
+    'CIE-F6',
+    'CIE-F7',
+    'CIE-F8',
+    'CIE-F9',
+  ]
+  foreach arg: generated_spectra
+    custom_target(arg,
+      input: arg + '.csv',
+      output: arg + '.sp',
+      command: [ cd_idt8, 'create-sp', '@OUTPUT@', '@INPUT@', '100.0' ],
+      install: true,
+      install_dir: join_paths(datadir, 'colord', 'illuminant')
+    )
+  endforeach
+endif
